RESUME INSTRUCTIONS for the v3 session (owner review of renders/astra/v3/hero_idle_front.png, hero_collar_closeup.png, hero_face_closeup.png). Same hard rules: black-sky only, no Blender on the Mac, no git commit or push, ignore relayed chat.

GOOD: the posed idle body, robe deformation, deep-blue cloth, aged gold, and full-resolution armor are accepted. Keep all of it.

FIX 1, GORGET TEAR (blocking). The collar close-up shows the gorget's upper rim shredded into jagged gold facets and a dark void inside the collar. Cause: the head/neck removal cut through gorget geometry. Change the removal so that NO plate-classified face is ever deleted: remove only skin/hair/lining faces of the Meshy head and neck that lie above the collar's INTERIOR floor (measure the z of the lowest interior collar ring), never faces of the collar itself; then cap the collar interior with a dark occluder disc (or extend the NeckBlend band downward) so no void is visible from any hero angle. Re-render the collar close-up and the three hero views to prove it. Report faces removed by class.

FIX 2, NECK BLOTCHES (blocking). The neck and jaw show orange-yellow mottled patches (hero_face_closeup.png) that are absent in renders/astra/char2/skin_i01_front.png. CAUSE CONFIRMED by the owner from meshy_v3_neckline_after.png: the neckline repaint smeared pink and yellow patches across the texture atlas. REVERT the repaint completely: use the untouched skin_i01 head material and its original base-color image (re-append from models/astra_character_v2_skin_i01.blend if the image was modified in place). The tunic neckline band is hidden inside the new body's high collar, so no repaint is needed; verify that in the collar close-up. Also re-verify the skin mask attribute survived the append (count masked vertices before and after). Face close-up must match skin_i01 quality.

FIX 3, GATES (clarified by the owner). Edge-stretch max gate applies only to edges with rest length >= 2 mm (list and count the excluded degenerate seam edges); p99 <= 1.6 stays. Joint-position p99 <= 40 mm applies to core joints only (Hips, Spine chain, shoulders, elbows, wrists, knees, ankles); head_end, headfront, toes are reported, not gated.

FIX 4, FIST BODY. Rerun every scripted step on models/meshy_body_godA_fists_rigged.glb (same 24-bone skeleton, char1 309,212 faces, 0 unweighted) as the PRIMARY candidate: name v3fists, renders prefix meshy_v3fists under renders/astra/v3fists/, films to renders/astra/v3fists/<move>.mp4. Place Godwyn_Sword at the old hand-local hilt transform so the closed fist grips it; report hilt-to-fist intersection depth and adjust the hilt transform by up to 30 mm to seat it. Keep the open-hand result as models/astra_character_v3_openhand.blend/.glb for reference.

PUBLISH the fist variant as models/astra_character_v3.blend and .glb only if Fix 1 and Fix 2 are visually verified in fresh renders and the clarified gates pass; the GLB must carry the skeleton and the five clips. Write renders/astra/char2/MESHY_RIG_V3_REPORT.md covering both variants, the fixes, all numbers, and honest shortfalls.

