codex
The preview proves the important source-geometry fix: the original gorget rim is continuous now, with no shredded gold facets, and the face/neck texture is clean rather than orange-mottled. It also exposed a new presentation defect from my occlusion solution: the rigid skin bridge reads as a rectangular block beside the collar in the full-body view. The dark cap itself is sufficient, so I’m removing that bridge and re-rendering; I’m not treating this first preview as publishable proof.
